    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 11 Walnut Avenue, Courtlands, Dublin 9  \r\n\r\nA spacious four-bedroom family home with a south-west facing rear garden, ideally positioned in a quiet cul-de-sac\r\nNo. 11 Walnut Avenue, Courtlands, Dublin 9 has just come to the market, and we are delighted to present this bright and spacious family home, extending to approximately 138.1 sq. m. (1,487 sq. ft.).\r\nOne of the many appealing features of this charming home is its peaceful cul-de-sac setting, offering a quiet and established residential environment. The property also enjoys a particularly attractive south-west facing rear garden, providing excellent afternoon and evening sunshine and offering wonderful potential for outdoor entertaining and family enjoyment.\r\nOn entering the property, you are welcomed by a bright entrance hall leading to a large front living room with fireplace, providing a generous and comfortable reception space.\r\nTo the rear is a second living room together with a separate dining room. The kitchen is conveniently positioned between the dining and living areas, creating a practical and well-proportioned layout for family living. A utility area to the rear provides additional convenience and storage.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the accommodation comprises four bedrooms, offering excellent flexibility for family living, home working or guest accommodation, together with a family bathroom.\r\nThe generous floor area of No 11, well-balanced accommodation and excellent location provide an excellent canvas for a purchaser to create a beautiful family home that reflects their own style and requirements.\r\nThe location is a particular highlight. Courtland Park is just a short stroll away, while an excellent selection of local amenities, neighbourhood shops, parks, primary and secondary schools and educational facilities are all within easy reach. Dublin City University is also conveniently located nearby.\r\nThe property is exceptionally well served by public transport, with an extensive Dublin Bus network available close by. The nearby R132/Drumcondra Road provides convenient access to Dublin City Centre, while the M50 motorway and Dublin Airport are also readily accessible."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "No. 11 Walnut Avenue offers a rare opportunity to acquire a spacious four-bedroom family home in a mature and highly convenient residential location. With its generous accommodation, peaceful cul-de-sac setting and sought-after south-west facing rear garden, the property provides an excellent foundation for a purchaser looking to modernise and create a home to their own taste and requirements."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Property Highlights\r\n•\tApproximately 138.1 sq. m. (1,487 sq. ft.)\r\n•\tFour-bedroom family home\r\n•\tTwo spacious double bedrooms and two additional bedrooms\r\n•\tBright entrance hall\r\n•\tLarge front living room with fireplace\r\n•\tAdditional rear living room\r\n•\tSeparate dining room\r\n•\tWell-positioned kitchen\r\n•\tUtility area\r\n•\tSouth-west facing rear garden\r\n•\tPeaceful cul-de-sac setting\r\n•\tEstablished and mature residential location\r\n•\tCourtland Park within a short stroll\r\n•\tExcellent selection of schools and colleges nearby\r\n•\tClose to Dublin City University\r\n•\tExcellent Dublin Bus services\r\n•\tConvenient access to Dublin City Centre, M50 and Dublin Airport\r\n•\tExcellent potential to create a superb family home"
